# .NET File Organization

- Prefer one top-level type per source file in the project.
- Do not declare reusable records, classes, structs, interfaces, or enums inline in `Program.cs` or unrelated files.
- Name each type file after the type it defines (for example, `RenameSummary.cs` for `RenameSummary`).
- Keep `Program.cs` focused on application flow and orchestration logic.
- If a type starts as local scaffolding and becomes shared or returned from methods, move it into its own file immediately.
